\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{Theory depends on exported operations and laws. Implementations may use Mathlib and definitional equality internally. Transparent finite shape syntax and the logical infrastructure of a bundled interface may compute; sealed categorical data may not.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{An abstraction boundary supports model changes. It does not by itself prove that a theorem generalizes: the interface hypotheses and comparison theorems do that.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{Depending on implementation equations in Theory; claiming every use of \code{rfl} is mathematically wrong. Reflexivity on interface expressions is legitimate.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{\ref{at-fd-0002}, the nonempty seal prototype and adversarial client.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{frozen policy; mechanism validated only by \ref{at-fd-0002}.}
}
